{"person_id":"candidate-04-01-richard-branson","name":"Richard Branson","cohort_group":"Founders / operators","category":"Business magnate / entrepreneur","birth_year":1950,"age_at_milestone":23,"milestone_by_age_26":"Founded Virgin Records label in 1973 at age 23 and released Mike Oldfield's Tubular Bells, a major commercial success that established Virgin as a significant music brand.","early_history_summary":"Branson launched Student magazine at age 16 in 1966 with Nik Powell, publishing the first issue in January 1968. By 1969 his net worth was estimated at £50,000. He pivoted from the magazine into a mail-order record business in 1970, opened his first record shop on Oxford Street in 1971, and launched the Virgin Records label in 1973, signing Mike Oldfield whose Tubular Bells became a massive hit.","primary_leverage_engine":"Execution / operations","normalized_primary_engine":"Execution / operations","secondary_engine":"Distribution / audience","started_serious_reps_before_20_score":1,"prior_reps_score":2,"scarce_skill_depth_score":1,"native_distribution_score":1,"elite_ecosystem_network_score":1,"complementary_team_score":1,"structural_wave_score":2,"concentration_intensity_score":1,"capital_safety_score":1,"domain_proximity_score":1,"total_leverage_score":12,"success_tier":1,"leverage_evidence_confidence":"High","family_context_summary":"Born into a middle-class English family in Surrey; father Edward was a barrister and mother Eve was a former ballet dancer and air hostess who supplemented family income with small entrepreneurial ventures. Branson attended the elite Stowe School but left at 16 due to poor academic performance linked to dyslexia.","parent_family_domain_summary":"Father was a barrister following family tradition; mother had entrepreneurial tendencies, making and selling wooden tissue boxes and waste paper bins, and encouraged independence and risk-taking in her children. No direct music or business-industry expertise transferred.","early_family_financial_platform_support_score":1,"parent_family_domain_advantage_score":0,"inherited_audience_business_network_score":0,"elite_institution_performance_pipeline_score":1,"frontier_geography_ecosystem_score":1,"rare_early_tools_facilities_score":0,"dedicated_mentor_coach_tutor_score":0,"exceptional_peer_cofounder_sibling_score":1,"early_online_platform_community_score":0,"direct_customer_domain_exposure_score":1,"prodigy_physical_edge_score":0,"adversity_constraint_catalyst_score":1,"inherited_access_stack_count":6,"exceptional_inherited_access_count":0,"all_documented_early_condition_count":6,"primary_early_advantage_archetype":"Self-created domain repetition","primary_early_advantage_tags":"early entrepreneurship, supportive family, London music scene, Stowe School, dyslexia-driven focus, complementary co-founder","evidence_summary":"Branson began serious entrepreneurial activity at 16, launching Student magazine and building a mail-order record business by 20. He rode the 1960s-70s music boom in London, a major cultural and commercial wave. His middle-class family provided modest safety and his mother modeled entrepreneurial behavior, but no significant inherited capital or industry networks were documented. His dyslexia and poor academic performance channeled him away from traditional careers and toward business from an early age. Nik Powell served as an early complementary co-founder on Student magazine. By 23, he had founded Virgin Records and released Tubular Bells, a landmark commercial success.","early_advantage_evidence_confidence":"Medium","source_count":4,"primary_source_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Branson","source_urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Branson","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_Richard_Branson%27s_business_ventures","https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/business/1986/11/16/virgin-records-pure-success-for-londoner/7fc7f96d-8b4c-48eb-9203-5237d14d07a9/","https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2014/sep/19/richard-branson-my-family-values"],"annotation_status":"subagent_researched_beta","source_audit_status":"not_independently_audited","data_version":"0.2.0-subagent-beta","eligibility_status":"age_26_eligible"}
